# id: parser.utf8-split-multibyte
# geometry: 20 2
# chunks: 4 2 6
# expect-line: 0 = café ─end
# expect-cursor: 0 9
#
# Multibyte UTF-8 split across feed boundaries must decode identically to the
# same bytes fed whole: a PTY delivers bytes in arbitrary read sizes and the
# parser may never let a split change what a sequence means. The first chunk
# ends between the two bytes of U+00E9; the third starts with the three-byte
# box-drawing U+2500 intact.
#
# Escapes: \e ESC, \r CR, \n LF, \t HT, \\ backslash, \xNN one byte.
# Every other character is emitted literally. Lines add no implicit newline.

caf\xc3
\xa9 \xe2\x94\x80end
